pixels r,g,b,a in sRGB; named colours as ImageRenderer resolves them (light)
white: [255, 255, 255, 255]
blue: [0, 122, 255, 255]
yellow: [255, 204, 0, 255]
cyan: [85, 190, 240, 255]

(1) ZStack { page; Color.blue.opacity(0.5); Color.yellow.blendMode(.multiply) }
blue at ½ over the white page: [128, 189, 255, 255]  (mix: [128, 189, 255])
over the white page: [128, 151, 0, 255]
  multiply(yellow, blue at ½ over page) = [128, 151, 0]
  multiply(yellow, opaque blue)         = [0, 98, 0]
over nothing (no page): [127, 150, 0, 255]
over a black page: [0, 49, 0, 255]  (multiply(yellow, blue at ½ over black) = [0, 49, 0])

(2) blended content over its own .background(Color.yellow)
text unblended over its fill (commonest): [([255, 255, 255, 255], 4344), ([255, 204, 0, 255], 1566), ([85, 190, 240, 255], 1024)]
text .blendMode(.multiply).background(yellow) over the page (commonest): [([255, 255, 255, 255], 4344), ([255, 204, 0, 255], 1566), ([85, 152, 0, 255], 1024)]
  multiply(cyan, yellow) = [85, 152, 0]
the same over an opaque blue (commonest): [([0, 122, 255, 255], 4344), ([255, 204, 0, 255], 1566), ([85, 152, 0, 255], 1024)]
  multiply(yellow, blue) = [0, 98, 0]
Color.cyan (20 wide) .blendMode(.multiply) .frame(40) .background(yellow), its middle: [85, 152, 0, 255]
the same over an opaque blue: under the cyan [85, 152, 0, 255], the fill beside it [255, 204, 0, 255]
